  "interpretation": {
    "conclusion": "The frozen normal-step cue does not separate the nominated collections. The enclosed-gap topology cue measures the team's reported missing-data observable, but a matched raw PHerc1447 control also contains enclosed gaps on every surface. No comparison establishes natural sheet-switch recall or specificity.",
    "reason": "The team describes PHerc1451's switches as black gaps, which are missing face-lattice data rather than coherent surface-normal discontinuities. The initial PHerc1451-versus-curated-PHerc1667 gap separation disappears as a presence/absence result under a raw-tracer control: PHerc1451 has gaps on 16 of 17 surfaces and PHerc1447 on 23 of 23. PHerc1451 has 3.32 times the gap-cell share but only 1.17 times the enclosed-region density, and neither raw collection has exact switch labels.",
    "limits": [
      "The PHerc1451 statement identifies a collection whose sheet switches should be visible as black gaps; it does not provide per-cell ground truth.",
      "The PHerc1667 statement excludes large-scale sheet switches only and explicitly notes a few outer half-wraps; it is not a cell-perfect clean label.",
      "PHerc1447 matches the raw z_dbg_gen output family but has no public clean or switch-free label; it controls pipeline family, not ground truth.",
      "The collections differ in scroll, pipeline, surface count, shape, and provenance; the result is a descriptive signature comparison, not a controlled accuracy estimate.",
      "The enclosed-gaps cue counts only invalid face-lattice components that do not connect to the grid boundary; it does not count open or boundary-connected black gaps.",
      "Cue cells are review locations, not classifications."
    ]
  },
